# Chapter 12 checkpoint. Start InventoryService, then the app:
#   dotnet run --project InventoryService
#   dotnet run --project AdventureWorks
# (two terminals, both from this folder; in Visual Studio, set
# both as startup projects). The app listens on
# https://localhost:7001, InventoryService on 127.0.0.1:42132.
# Each "Expect" line is the status you should see. Send them in
# order, within a minute of starting the app: the resilience
# requests count attempts and depend on the breaker's history.

@host = https://localhost:7001
@inventory = http://127.0.0.1:42132

###
# Start the warehouse stand-in clean. Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/reset

###
# Output caching. The first read runs the endpoint.
# Expect 200, and it has no Age header
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/1

###
# The second comes from the output cache. Expect 200, and it
# has an Age header
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/1

###
# The public catalog is compressed.
# Expect 200, and it carries Content-Encoding: br
GET {{host}}/api/catalog
Accept-Encoding: br

###
# Other routes are not. Expect 200, and it has no
# Content-Encoding header
GET {{host}}/api/status
Accept-Encoding: br

###
# Warehouse stock through the distributed cache: a miss, so one
# call to InventoryService. Expect 200 with "available": 42
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/1/availability

###
# Expect 200 with {"attempts":1}
GET {{inventory}}/control/attempts

###
# A hit: no call. Expect 200 with "available": 42
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/1/availability

###
# Still one attempt. Expect 200 with {"attempts":1}
GET {{inventory}}/control/attempts

###
# The next two stock calls fail with 503. Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/fail/2

###
# Two retries absorb both failures. Expect 200 with
# "available": 17
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/2/availability

###
# One plus three attempts. Expect 200 with {"attempts":4}
GET {{inventory}}/control/attempts

###
# A 400 is permanent. Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/status/400

###
# Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/fail/1

###
# No retry for a 400. Expect 503
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/3/availability

###
# One more attempt only. Expect 200 with {"attempts":5}
GET {{inventory}}/control/attempts

###
# Now every call fails with 503. Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/reset

###
# Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/fail/100

###
# This failure makes three of the last six attempts (half) fail,
# so the circuit breaker opens, and the retries fail fast.
# Expect 503
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/4/availability

###
# One attempt reached the service. Expect 200 with
# {"attempts":1}
GET {{inventory}}/control/attempts

###
# While the breaker is open, no call reaches the service.
# Expect 503
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/4/availability

###
# Expect 200 with {"attempts":1}
GET {{inventory}}/control/attempts

###
# Expect 204
POST {{inventory}}/control/reset

###
# Rate limiting: five searches per ten seconds for each client.
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# The sixth is refused. Expect 429, and it has a Retry-After
# header
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# A signed-in user has a partition of her own. Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/casey

###
# Expect 200
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/search?q=trail

###
# Eviction: the Admin changes a price. Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/avery

###
# Expect 204
PUT {{host}}/api/v2/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Trail Helmet", "price": 31.99 }

###
# Expect 204
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-out

###
# The write evicted the "catalog" tag, so this read runs the
# endpoint again. Expect 200 with "price": 31.99, and it has no
# Age header
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/1

###
# Put the price back. Expect 200
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-in/avery

###
# Expect 204
PUT {{host}}/api/v2/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Trail Helmet", "price": 29.99 }

###
# Expect 204
POST {{host}}/dev/sign-out

###
# Expect 200 with "price": 29.99
GET {{host}}/api/catalog/1
